From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lance-linalg: add a portable riscv64 SIMD fallback

lance-linalg's f32x8/f32x16/i32x8/f64x4/f64x8 SIMD types
(src/simd/{f32,f64,i32}.rs) are defined, and every trait impl for them
written, only under `#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64"/"aarch64"/
"loongarch64")]` -- unlike u8x16/u8x32 (src/simd/u8.rs), which already
carry a portable fallback. riscv64 hits "cannot find type `f32x8` in
this scope" as soon as lance-linalg (a dependency of lance, which
crates/lance-context-core depends on directly) is built. Add the same
shape of fallback for the three missing types: an array-backed struct
plus a scalar implementation of every method the SIMD/FloatSimd traits
require, gated `#[cfg(not(any(target_arch = "x86_64", target_arch =
"aarch64", target_arch = "loongarch64")))]` beside the existing
per-architecture arms, which are otherwise untouched. Add/Sub/Mul on
i32x8 use wrapping arithmetic to match the silent-wraparound semantics
of the SIMD instructions they replace.

Applied (via patches/lance-context/0.6.5/0003-cargo-patch-lance-crates-for-riscv64.patch)
to a local copy of this crate's 7.0.0 crates.io release, which
crates/lance-context-core's `lance = "7.0.0"` pulls in transitively
and cannot be patched in place (CLAUDE.md gotcha 300).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to lance-format/lance]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/src/simd/f32.rs b/src/simd/f32.rs
